   "id": "shabbat.94a.5",
   "daf": "94a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "אֶת הַמֵּת בַּמִּטָּה חַיָּיב וְכֵן כְּזַיִת מִן הַמֵּת וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן, וְאָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף אָמַר רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן לָקִישׁ: פּוֹטֵר הָיָה רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna that according to the first tanna: One who carries out «a corpse on a bed is liable. And similarly,» one who carries out «an olive-bulk of a corpse,» or an olive-bulk of an animal carcass, or a lentil-bulk of a creeping animal is liable. Rabbi Shimon deems him exempt. «Rabba bar bar Ḥana said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said, and Rav Yosef said» that «Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish said: Rabbi Shimon would deem exempt»"
  }
 ],
